   <layout class="QGridLayout" name="gridLayout_6">
    <item row="0" column="0">
     <!-- P5.1 (2026-10-08): collapsed scrollLeft + leftPanel.
          Previously this QScrollArea (350 px wide) sat in centralWidget
          column 0 but only contained an empty leftPanel since Q4.2.2
          migrated MosaicTool/TextOverlay settings out. The dock column
          (LeftToolBar + ModeSelectorBar + ImageOptionBar) already
          occupies Qt::LeftDockWidgetArea, so centralWidget has nothing to
          show on the left. The 350-px chrome became ~30% wasted horizontal
          space, visually inflating every docked widget. Setting width to
          0 collapses the column; verticalLayout in row 0 col 1 then fills
          the freed horizontal space for the canvas. -->
